<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gosamaru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1458">1458</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gosamaru was a Ryukyuan lord and military commander of the fifteenth century, known for building the castle of Zakimi and strengthening Nakagusuku. In 1458 his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amawari">Amawari</a>, lord of Katsuren, accused him of plotting rebellion; royal forces attacked Nakagusuku and Gosamaru took his own life. Amawari's own revolt was then crushed, an episode later retold in Ryukyuan drama.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His First Sho dynasty proved unstable: after a series of short reigns and the <b>Gosamaru</b>–Amawari conflict of 1458, the royal treasurer Kanemaru seized power on the death of Sho Toku and was proclaimed king as Sho En in 1470, founding the Second Sho dynasty, which reigned until 1879.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ryukyu-kingdom">Ryukyu Kingdom · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
